    <title>Daily Digest 2026-11-27: Show HN: Scolast – AI tutor for autodidacts inspir; Temporal and Durable Execution for AI Agents; Introducing the llama.cpp benchmark dashboard for </title>
    <updated>2026-11-27T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://islandirie.github.io/my-rss-feed/daily/2026-11-27.html"/>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Scolast – AI tutor for autodidacts inspired by Bloom's 2 sigma problem&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://scolast.com"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Temporal and Durable Execution for AI Agents&lt;/b&gt; — Design patterns and lessons from production systems — high-leverage reading for senior engineers. &lt;a href="https://softwareengineeringdaily.com/podcasts/temporal-and-durable-execution-for-ai-agents/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Introducing the llama.cpp benchmark dashboard for AMD Ryzen and Radeon&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Google Will Make AI Agents Use Its MCP Servers. The Gmail One Can't Send Email&lt;/b&gt; — Expanding what LLMs can interact with — relevant if you're building or using agentic pipelines. &lt;a href="https://techstackups.com/articles/google-workspace-ai-agents-mcp/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: DataFluxor – SEO, Etsy Research and Scraping via API and MCP&lt;/b&gt; — Expanding what LLMs can interact with — relevant if you're building or using agentic pipelines. &lt;a href="https://datafluxor.com"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Quoting Jack Despain Zhou&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/26/jack-despain-zhou/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Swarms, Flocks, Gangs: How to build, train, and evaluate multi-agent systems&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://huggingface.co/blog/training-swarms"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sandboxes, secure inference, and keeping agents from going rogue&lt;/b&gt; — Flagged as relevant to your interests — read the summary to decide if it's worth your time. &lt;a href="https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/11/27/sandboxes-secure-inference-and-rogue-agents/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
